4.28.m:
Thus this eulogy of Vaidyanātheśvara has been proclaimed;
for people who hear it, sin is turned to ashes.

Thus ends the twenty-eighth chapter, titled 'Description of the Eulogy of the Vaidyanātheśvara Jyotirliṅga,' in the fourth Koṭirudrasaṃhitā of the glorious Śiva Mahāpurāṇa.

4.29.m:
Sūta said:
Hearing those words of hers, the rākṣasas became joyful;
all those rākṣasas, now fearless, said to one another then:
